# The pinned ingredients of the certified combination, in ONE place.
#
# Everything that says "which solver, which bytes" for a release lives here and
# nowhere else.  Two repositories read this file:
#
#   * this fork's CI -- .github/scripts/solver-pins.sh is sourced by
#     release-fetch-cvc5.sh, release-build-unix.sh, release-smoke.sh and
#     release-attach.sh, and .github/workflows/main.yml exports the win-64 row
#     into the PowerShell cvc5 step;
#   * isabelle-packaging-ci's conda/components/isabelle-nunchaku/recipe.yaml,
#     which checks out this fork at the release tag and dies unless its own five
#     `sha256:` literals, its cvc5/smbc versions and its subdir->platform table
#     all agree with the records below.
#
# Why a data file rather than two synchronised tables of literals: before this
# file existed, cvc5 1.3.4 was pinned by ten independent literals across the two
# repositories with nothing comparing them, so a security bump applied to one
# side would have shipped a combination that was never smoked, with every gate
# green (measured during the 2026-08-25 pipeline review: the ten literals were
# equal that day purely by hand).
#
# FORMAT.  One record per line; `#` starts a comment; fields are whitespace
# separated.  A selector must match exactly one line -- solver-pins.sh fails
# loudly on a missing or duplicated record, which is what makes a half-applied
# edit here a red leg instead of a mixed release.
#
#   cvc5-version   <version>
#   smbc-version   <version>
#   smbc-commit    <40-hex commit the smbc version tag resolved to>
#   cvc5 <isabelle-platform> <release-asset-basename> <sha256-of-the-zip>
#
# The `cvc5` records are also the fork's definition of WHICH FIVE PLATFORMS a
# release covers: the release-gate job builds its expected asset list from them.

# cvc5 >= 1.3.1 is required: the backend sends get-model-domain-elements, which
# older cvc5 answers with an error.
cvc5-version   1.3.4

# smbc 0.6.1 is the version regress/README.md section 2 certifies.  Changing it
# is a re-certification event.
smbc-version   0.6.1

# The commit `v0.6.1` resolved to, measured 2026-08-25 against the GitHub API
# (/repos/c-cube/smbc/git/ref/tags/v0.6.1 -- a LIGHTWEIGHT tag, so the ref sha is
# the commit itself).  A git tag is mutable: upstream can re-cut it, and because
# smbc stamps its --version from smbc.opam's `version:` field the binary would
# still say 0.6.1 and every version assertion would still pass.  This line is
# the only thing that pins the bytes.  Both job families check it: the unix legs
# hand it to `opam pin` as the fragment, the win-64 leg asserts `git rev-parse
# HEAD` against it after the shallow tag clone.
smbc-commit    87a5a750b5f0b2d7e1ef2459a8e62f07ed54e0d5

# The five official static cvc5 release assets, one per Isabelle platform.
# Digests measured 2026-08-25 against the cvc5-1.3.4 release.  The asset name is
# paired with the platform HERE, so a matrix edit cannot pair an x86_64 cvc5
# with an arm64 leg -- that pairing used to live in the workflow matrix, where
# nothing cross-checked it.
cvc5  x86_64-linux   cvc5-Linux-x86_64-static   dcdbfada0ce493ee98259c0816e0daafc561c223aadb3af298c2968e73ea39c6
cvc5  arm64-linux    cvc5-Linux-arm64-static    2a4c108367f20b0c8990abd6b9535a5d62e08908d471d4671c00734e408f85bc
cvc5  x86_64-darwin  cvc5-macOS-x86_64-static   5a7976affaf37dcf03ee44c3d0297c8e0ba08afd44ac832dab97400da726b852
cvc5  arm64-darwin   cvc5-macOS-arm64-static    3840aa53f6ee6fc357415dcfe291d7f5ffec6cfb1ccca6fef64120a0d2be4cb6
cvc5  x86_64-cygwin  cvc5-Win64-x86_64-static   279fe7e95810cfb62433fcfc2932f35325a665f32d3697ff33f75e31d5c6a179
